{
  "case_id": "2020-19-251",
  "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0000-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Disclosure of their Schedule Bs, the petitioners alleged, would make their donors less likely to contribute and would subject them to the risk of reprisals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In their complaints, they alleged that the Attorney General had violated their First Amendment rights and the rights of their donors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Ninth Circuit again vacated the District Court's injunctions, and this time reversed the judgments and remanded for entry of judgment in favor of the Attorney General."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0001-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Judge Ikuta dissented, joined by four other judges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Foundation and Law Center",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Foundation and the Law Center both argued below that the obligation to disclose Schedule Bs to the Attorney General was unconstitutional on its face and as applied to them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The upshot is that California casts a dragnet for sensitive donor information from tens of thousands of charities each year, even though that information will become relevant in only a small number of cases involving fled complaints."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We are left to conclude that the Attorney General's disclosure requirement imposes a widespread burden on donors' associational rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0002-0006",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority holds that a California regulation requiring charitable organizations to disclose tax forms containing the names and contributions of their top donors unconstitutionally burdens the right to associate even if the forms are not publicly disclosed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0003-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Today, the Court abandons the requirement that plaintiffs demonstrate that they are chilled, much less that they are reasonably chilled. Instead, it presumes (contrary to the evidence, precedent, and common sense) that all disclosure requirements impose associational burdens. For example, the Court explains that there is a risk of chill in this suit because the government requires disclosure of the identity of any donor \u201cwith reason to remain anonymous.\u201d Ante, at 617."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0004-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In any event, the Court need not read a few isolated sen-\ntences from that opinion to divine Shelton's meaning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of California",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California's Schedule B regulation, however, is a nonpublic reporting requirement, and California has implemented security measures to ensure that Schedule B information remains confdential."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Nearly a quarter of the country's charitable assets are held by charities registered in California."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Today's decision discards decades of First Amendment jurisprudence recognizing that reporting and disclosure requirements do not directly burden associational rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-19-251",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "870c1348d5ac06f36fdbf074f56424987b755a1139c15dc60c1d5230240b5515",
      "evidence_id": "ev-870c1348d5ac-0005-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These moves are wholly inconsistent with the Court's precedents and our Court's long-held view that disclosure requirements only indirectly burden First Amendment rights."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
